s and customs guided daily life. Rules helped people understand accepted community practices.", "Social relationships. Cooperation between rulers and people supported stability. Stability depended on relationships between rulers and their people.", "A tradition of learning. Family education and formal education had already developed. Knowledge was passed through families and places of learning."], "text": "Organised government. Local communities already had systems of administration. These systems existed before Western powers arrived. Local leadership. Rulers, chiefs and village heads each had their own roles. Leaders had responsibilities at different levels of administration. Community rules. Written laws and customs guided daily life. Rules helped people understand accepted community practices. Social relationships. Cooperation between rulers and people supported stability. Stability depended on relationships between rulers and their people. A tradition of learning. Family education and formal education had already developed. Knowledge was passed through families and places of learning."}